# Cloudflare Pages (and Netlify) SPA fallback.
#
# React Router resolves /result and /how-it-works in the browser, so the
# host never has files at those paths. Without this, opening a shared
# result link directly - or refreshing on one - returns 404, which is the
# common way a client-side-routed deploy breaks only in production.
#
# 200, not 301: the URL must stay as the visitor typed it so the router can
# read it (and /result reads its whole profile from the query string).
/*    /index.html   200
